# Git Workflow Rules

## Data Safety

- Do not ask git to process files larger than 50 MB.
- Do not use `git lfs`, `git filter-repo`, or force-push unless the user explicitly asks and the risk is reviewed.
- Never use destructive reset/checkout commands to discard user changes unless explicitly requested.

## Before Commit

- Check the diff and confirm only intended files changed.
- Treat `appendix/qa.tex` as high-value content; inspect carefully before staging.
- Keep generated PDFs and large assets out of commits unless the user specifically wants them tracked.

## Docker

- Never run `docker compose down -v` or `docker compose rm -v`.
- Prefer `docker restart <container>` or `docker compose down` without `-v`.
